IED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:12157","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-1. E sta b lish m en t o f the C ouncil.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-1","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-101. There is hereby established the President’s Management Improvement  \nCouncil.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-101","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-101","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-102. The Council shall be Cochaired by the Director of the Office of  \nManagement and Budget and the Director of the Office of Personnel Manage­\nment. The Council’s membership shall consist of representatives from Execu­\ntive agencies and from the non-Federal sector; such as business, industry,  \norganized labor, foundations, universities, and State and local governments.  \nThe members shall be appointed by the President.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-102","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-102","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-2. F u n ctio n s o f  the C ouncil.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-2","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-201. The Council shall advise the President on significant and critical  \nmanagement problems and issues affecting Executive agencies and Govern­\nment programs.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-201","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-201","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-202. The Council shall work cooperatively with the Comptroller General,  \nsenior program management and administrative officials, and Inspectors Gen­\neral to provide advice and guidance on specific management improvement  \nprojects involving one or more Executive agencies.\n1— 203. Where feasible, the Council shall advise the Executive agencies in the  \ndevelopment of management systems or management techniques to improve  \nthe effectiveness and responsiveness of Federal programs.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-202","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-202","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-204. The Council shall advise the Executive agencies of solutions to critical  \nmanagement problems, as well as the constraints on management effective­\nness.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-204","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-204","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-205. In developing its recommendations, the Council shall utilize the experi­\nence of the public and private sectors. The Council shall also identify and  \nfacilitate the application to Federal programs of appropriate successful sys­\ntems and techniques which have been used elsewhere in the public and  \nprivate sectors.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-205","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-205","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-206. The Cochairmen shall report to the President on the performance of the  \nCouncil’s functions.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-206","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-206","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-301. The-Director of the Office of Personnel Management shall, to the extent  \npermitted by law, provide the Council with administrative and staff services,  \nsupport and facilities as may be necessary for the effective performance of its  \nfunctions.\n\n=== PDF page 14 of 264 ===\n54036 Federal Register /  Vol. 44, No. 182 /  Tuesday, September 18, 1979 /  Presidential Documents\nFR D oc. 79-29065 \nFiled 9-14-79; 3:15 p m ] \nB illing code 3195-01-M\n1-302. Each member of the Council, who is not otherwise a full-time employee  \nof the Federal Government, shall receive no compensation from the United  \nStates by virtue of their service on the Council, but all members may receive  \nthe transportation and travel expenses, including per diem in lieu of subsist­\nence, authorized by law (5 U.S.C. 5702 and 5703).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-301","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-301","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-401. Notwithstanding the provisions of any other Executive order, the  \nfunctions of the President under the Federal Advisory Committee Act (5 U.S.C.  \nApp. I), except that of reporting annually to the Congress, shall be performed  \nby the Director of the Office of Personnel Management in accordance with  \nguidelines and procedures established by the Administrator of General Serv­\nices.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-401","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-401","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-402. The Council shall terminate on December 31, 1980, unless sooner  \nextended.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-402","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12157#sec1-402","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"44 FR 54035, PDF pages 13-14","sha256":"cfd1c97f161844b6209ab70359a404c46a75cc46b00da545656cc7358c25da9a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1979-09-18/pdf/FR-1979-09-18.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 12 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:12157"}
